<title>HUNGARY: Hungary revises Jan household savings figures.</title>
<headline>Hungary revises Jan household savings figures.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's net household savings rose 42.5 billion forints in January according to revised figures published by the National Bank of Hungary on Wednesday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY HOUSEHOLD SAVINGS (in billion forints)</p>
<p>				 Jan '97	 Dec '96	Jan' 96</p>
<p> Forint savings	    2,280.7	 2,250.0	1,774.0</p>
<p> Foreign currency	    478.9	   475.4	  447.0</p>
<p> Total savings	     2,769.6	 2,725.4	2,221.0</p>
<p> Total loans		   334.5	   342.8	  367.5</p>
<p> Net household savings   2,425.1	 2,382.6	1,853.5 @</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are not inflation adjusted. December 1996 and January 1997 figures are preliminary. Consumer price inflation was 18.9 percent year-on-year in January. Previously the NBH said household savings rose 33.3 billion forints in January, but revised it on the bases of an analysis of bank securities' maturities.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042</p>
